{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 live stop test 2 (operator, 2026-11-04 PST): agent stopped 15:17:07, rebar-host-logs-not-arriving ALARM only at 15:43:54 (26 min 47 s), missing the 15-minute bound. Root cause, from the alarm's own history: the ALARM evaluation used buckets 15:28/15:33/15:38; with 300 s x 3 and no FILL, CloudWatch evaluates the most recent REAL datapoints inside its 5-datapoint evaluation range, so the last healthy 15:13 bucket held the alarm OK until it aged out (AWS alarm docs, evaluation range). Fix: FILL(m, 0) over 60 s periods, 10 of 10. Read-only checks: get-metric-data with FILL returns real zeros for every stopped minute, including a window with no real datapoint; on-box journal over 14 days had entries in every minute but one isolated empty minute, so 10 empty minutes does not occur when healthy. Stop test 1 was invalidated by the hourly configure association restarting the agent at 15:00:31; runbook now documents that self-heal and how to time a stop test. The empty /nginx journald stream is expected: nginx.service writes to the journal only at startup (24 config-test lines since 2026-09-06); runtime errors are in /nginx-error."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793836729765510001,"uuid":"b4dc4784-6f3e-41bc-917b-f664b7d10065"}